From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:31:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/25] [GLM5Next] Write KDA prefill q, k, v as separate dense
 tensors

GLM-5.3-Flash's KDA prefill runs one merged short conv over q|k|v and
splits the [T, 3 * P] output into three views with a 3 * P token stride.
The prefill kernel needs dense q, k and v, so each KDA layer copied three
[T, P] tensors per chunk (three 56 MB copies per layer at 16k tokens).

causal_conv1d_fn gains an out_group argument: when set, the kernel
stores features into a [dim // out_group, seqlen, out_group] output, so
each group comes out as its own dense tensor. KDA passes
out_group=local_projection_size and unbinds. Only the store address
changes, so the outputs are bit-identical; other callers keep
out_group=0 and the old layout.

Source: kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10 @ c748079,
  experimental/fixes/causal_conv1d.py and the prefill hunk of
  experimental/fixes/kda.py (base vLLM ddd6fbca), by Matt Mastracci
  (also mmastrac/glm-5.3-flash-4x-gx10 PR #4); porting authorized by the
  owner. knapcio's overlay/glm_kda_conv_split.py (MIT) is an independent
  wrapper implementation of the same idea and was not used.
Upstream: absent in v0.31.0 and main. The related strided KDA recurrent
  inputs (knapcio glm_kda_nocopy) are already in v0.31.0 (1768273c1).
Claimed gain: Kindling (4x GB10, TP=4): prefill +2-3%. knapcio (4x GB10,
  TP=4): the copies were 47 ms of a 2554 ms 5760-row prefill chunk
  (1.8%).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
